      "slug": "rigging-and-skinning",
      "title": "Rigging & Skinning",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.luccote.com/rigging-and-skinning",
      "text": [
        {
          "kind": "h1",
          "text": "Rigging and Skinning"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Driven Key Skeleton"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "This is an example of using extra \"Driven Key\" bones in a Maya skeleton, and the comparison of their benefits. On the left is a standard skeleton with no helper bones, and on the right, my improved skeleton with improved deformations."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "During LA Noire we used a specific Driven Key skeleton for complex motions, animation assistance and corrections. For Project WOTO, I dropped the extra bone count from 56 to merely 18, not only holding the same deformations, but improving them greatly as well."
        }
      ],
